## Goal
Write the memo for the Platform team weekly of 2026-10-19 from the notes file /private/tmp/hirearchy-g0-m1-s3-1793003475/notes/2026-10-19.md (read-only; read that file only). Write it with hirearchy write to lead/writer/work/memo-2026-10-19.md (the final file; name the path in your report).

Guidance from earlier cases: the memo opens with one line starting 'Summary:'; then the decisions section; then the action-items table (Owner | Action | Due). Quote the notes' own words for preferences/offers, do not strengthen them. 'for <date>' / 'on <date>' = event or action date as stated; where the notes give no deadline Due is none. Turn vague deadlines (e.g. 'end of next week', 'before Friday') into a date counted from the meeting date (Monday 2026-10-19) only when the notes make it clear, and state the derivation in a short 'Open questions' line (counted in the word limit); otherwise Due is none. Scan the whole notes for informal commitments in prose (e.g. someone 'will', 'said he'd', 'offered to'), not only ACTION lines, each with the right owner. Decisions must include every decision in the notes (also logistics ones). Nothing from outside the notes.

Acceptance criteria (verbatim):
- C1: Covers only the meeting in the requested notes file, and nothing that is not in that file.
- C2: At most 400 words.
- C3: Has a section listing the decisions taken in the meeting, and every decision in the notes is listed.
- C4: Has the action items as a markdown table with exactly the columns Owner | Action | Due.
- C5: Every commitment in the notes is a row in the table, including informal ones that someone only mentioned in prose (not only lines labelled ACTION), each with the right owner.
- C6: Every Due value is an ISO date (YYYY-MM-DD). A vague deadline (such as before Friday, end of next week, the next meeting) is turned into a date counted from the meeting date when the notes make it clear; otherwise Due is none.
- C8: The memo starts with a one-line 'Summary:' of the meeting, followed by the decisions section, then the action items table, in that order.
(C7: the reviewer will check; you apply every required change.)

Regression list (client rejections, verbatim):
